ce them, but the main message must be oneOf.indexes.', 'description': 'When more than one schema validates and canShortCircuit() returns true, the loop breaks after the second match; the validator must still report a oneOf.indexes error because numberOfValidSchema != 1.'}]}, {'group': 'No discriminator – multiple schemas validate, short‑circuit NOT allowed', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': 'mock ExecutionContext (failFast=false, discriminator disabled)'}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'JSON node that satisfies three schemas'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'same as node'}, {'parameter': 'instanceLocation', 'value': 'JsonNodePath.root()'}, {'parameter': 'walk', 'value': 'true'}], 'expected': 'ValidationMessage set containing a single message with key "oneOf.indexes", arguments "3" and "0, 1, 2" (three valid schemas). Loop iterates over all schemas because canShortCircuit() returns false.', 'description': 'Ensures the validator does not break early when short‑circuiting is disabled and still reports a oneOf.indexes error.'}]}, {'group': 'Discriminator enabled – matching discriminator found', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': 'mock ExecutionContext (failFast=true, discriminator enabled, DiscriminatorContext active)'}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'JSON node with property "type":"A" (discriminator property present)'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'same as node'}, {'parameter': 'instanceLocation', 'value': 'JsonNodePath.root()'}, {'parameter': 'walk', 'value': 'false'}], 'expected': 'empty ValidationMessage set if the schema referenced by "$ref" matches the discriminator value; otherwise a oneOf error as in the non‑discriminator case.', 'description': 'When discriminator is enabled and the node contains the discriminator property that maps to a $ref of the currently evaluated schema, the validator marks a match, collects child errors only from the matching schema and ultimately returns no error if that schema validates.'}]}, {'group': 'Discriminator enabled – discriminator property missing (ignore path)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': 'mock ExecutionContext (failFast=false, discriminator enabled, DiscriminatorContext active)'}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'JSON node without the discriminator property'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'same as node'}, {'parameter': 'instanceLocation', 'value': 'JsonNodePath.root()'}, {'parameter': 'walk', 'value': 'true'}], 'expected': 'ValidationMessage set containing a oneOf error (same rules as without discriminator) because the context is marked as ignore and childErrors are aggregated from all schemas.', 'description': 'If the discriminator property is absent, the context is marked ignore; the validator must fall back to normal handling and report a oneOf error when the number of valid schemas is not exactly one.'}]}, {'group': 'Discriminator enabled – no matching schema and not ignored', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': 'mock ExecutionContext (failFast=true, discriminator enabled, DiscriminatorContext active)'}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'JSON node with discriminator property "type":"UNKNOWN" that does not match any $ref'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'same as node'}, {'parameter': 'instanceLocation', 'value': 'JsonNodePath.root()'}, {'parameter': 'walk', 'value': 'false'}], 'expected': 'ValidationMessage set containing a single message built from message().instanceNode(...).arguments("based on the provided discriminator. No alternative could be chosen based on the discriminator property")', 'description': 'When discriminator is enabled, a discriminator validator exists, but none of the schemas match the discriminator value, the validator must produce the special error indicating that no alternative could be chosen.'}]}]
